MODULE 18: LECTURER / TRAINER PORTAL
HI-TECH College Integrated Digital Academic & Certification Platform
Module specification Role-based portal

The Lecturer / Trainer Portal is the central workspace for lecturers, trainers, instructors, practical assessors and approved teaching staff. It enables them to manage their teaching responsibilities, students, learning materials, assessments, examinations, marking, academic feedback and departmental communication.

The portal must work on desktop, tablet and mobile devices.

1. Lecturer dashboard
Every lecturer receives a personalized dashboard showing only their assigned teaching responsibilities and permitted records.

Dashboard components:

Total assigned courses, units and classes.

Total students under their teaching responsibility.

Today's lessons and upcoming classes.

Weekly teaching timetable.

Pending attendance records.

CATs and assignments awaiting marking.

Upcoming examinations and practical assessments.

Pending results submissions.

Student questions and support requests.

Pending HOD approvals.

Recent announcements and notifications.

Teaching workload summary.

Quick access to notes, schemes of work and lesson plans.

Dashboard shortcuts:

Create lesson plan.

Upload learning material.

Record attendance.

Create CAT.

Create assignment.

Create examination.

Mark submissions.

Submit results.

Contact students.

Request timetable adjustment.

