41. Security and access control
The lecturer role must have the following restrictions:

Cannot create or delete institutional staff identities.

Cannot change their own staff registration number.

Cannot assign themselves courses or classes.

Cannot approve their own results where independent approval is required.

Cannot publish official examination results without authorization.

Cannot access other departments' restricted records without permission.

Cannot change approved timetables directly.

Cannot access confidential HR, finance or counselling records by default.

Cannot view another student's private assessment feedback.

Cannot execute untrusted student code on the main application server.

All assessment, marking, result and attendance changes must be auditable.

42. Acceptance criteria
The Lecturer Portal should only be considered implemented when:

Lecturer login and role-based access work.

Lecturer accounts link to existing staff records.

Staff registration numbers display correctly.

Department and campus restrictions are enforced by the backend.

Teaching assignments are visible and accurate.

Lecturers can create lesson plans and schemes of work.

Learning materials can be uploaded and accessed by assigned students.

Attendance can be recorded and audited.

CATs and assignments can be created and submitted.

Question banks can be managed.

Assessment marking works for supported question types.

Practical and programming submissions are securely handled.

Results can be submitted and moderated.

Published results are protected from unauthorized editing.

Student feedback remains private.

Notifications work through configured channels.

Mobile layouts and essential workflows function.

Automated tests cover role restrictions and critical workflows.

